      "writtenOn": "2023-05-25T14:56:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I also prefer STL types, but they do yield more bloated code than Skia containers.  So we tend to begrudgingly stick to Skia equivalents:\n\n  std::vector -\u003e TArray\n  std::pair -\u003e struct ValuePair { ... }\n  std::unordered_map -\u003e THashMap\n  std::string -\u003e SkString",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 60,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 66,
        "endChar": 74
      },
      "revId": "ed4e6716f0d9cee82755af00bc80919f5929b043",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "002dfb42_112737f5",
        "filename": "modules/skottie/include/SlotManager.h",
        "patchSetId": 5
      },
      "lineNbr": 73,
      "author": {
        "id": 5642
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-05-25T14:56:34Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This is kind of iffy, because the JSON dom is only valid during parsing while the SlotManager will presumably persist -- so we end up with a dangling pointer.\n\nI don\u0027t see it being used by the SlotManager itself, just AnimationBuilder for parsing initial slot values.  Maybe it should stay in AnimationBuilder for now?",
      "revId": "ed4e6716f0d9cee82755af00bc80919f5929b043",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
